  "question": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\left(\\frac{e^{2 x}-1}{e^{2 x}+1}\\right)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ivzax",
      "text": "an increasing function",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NKMqd",
      "text": "a decreasing function",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "esMcK",
      "text": "an even function",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wdpwC",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\because \\mathrm{f}(x)=\\left(\\frac{e^{2 x}-1}{e^{2 x}+1}\\right) \\\\\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\mathrm{f}(-x)=\\frac{e^{-2 x}-1}{e^{-2 x}+1}=\\frac{1-e^{2 x}}{1+e^{2 x}} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}(-x)=\\frac{-\\left(e^{2 x}-1\\right)}{e^{2 x}+1}=-\\mathrm{f}(x)\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{f}(x)$ is an odd function.\r\n\r\nAgain, $\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{4 e^{2 x}}{\\left(1+e^{2 x}\\right)^{2}}>0, \\forall x \\in R$ $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}(x)$ is an increasing function.",
    "image": null
